# kprompt CLI rules

## Repo

Public Go CLI + Observe agent (`github.com/kprompt/kprompt`). See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/dev.md`.

## Product constraints

- PlanResult → approve → apply. No silent cluster mutate.
- Observe / agent: propose / notify first; Autopilot only behind explicit policy gates.
- Hard-deny wipe-class intents; be careful with `--approve` in docs and demos.
- Do not commit secrets, API keys, or kubeconfigs.

## Commands

```bash
go test ./...
go build -o bin/kprompt ./cmd/kprompt
# kind E2E when needed:
go test -tags=e2e ./test/e2e/ -count=1 -v -timeout 10m
```

Prefer package-scoped tests while iterating.

## Style

- `gofmt`; packages under `internal/`; Cobra commands under `cmd/kprompt`.
- Agent edits to `*.go` are auto-formatted by the project `afterFileEdit` hook when enabled.
- Match existing error/UI patterns in `internal/ui` and neighboring packages.
- Update `docs/*.md` when flags or behavior change.
- No drive-by refactors; keep PRs focused.

## Commits

Only commit or open PRs when the user asks.
